This publication checkout preserves the public upstream history and introduces
the qualified local engine as a curated change. Private installation history is
not included. release/engine-source.json records file hashes and the measured
source identity; benchmarks/ contains selected, sanitized historical summaries.
The portable deployment tooling is new and requires separate hardware qualification.

The October 2026 local integration selectively ports Bertholomus v0.5 changes
(release 508bfb34743f88d35abcb514f7013ef531ce34a5, reviewed at 808eb4a1090ca7b79173cc2c799de16da5f923e3)
into the family ops, model, kernels, graph and round code and the already listed
EXL3 expert files. It adds the associated correctness probes under tools/dsv41/.
Local adaptations preserve request-bounded positional tables, explicit decode
workspace and bounded retained state. Source attribution and scope are in
tools/dsv41/ATTRIBUTION.md and deployment/UPSTREAM-V05.md; the framework remains
based on TensorFold 0.6.3 rather than a complete 0.6.6 merge.

The v0.5.1 integration selectively ports Bertholomus commits dfbe519, 741a507 and
90b68e0: a family FP32 startup check and an opt-in reasoning-loop guard. The local
adaptation previews multiple loop windows per callback, checks guard eligibility
before tokenizer lookup, and preserves local sampling and grammar behavior.
deployment/UPSTREAM-V051.md records the source commits, scope and validation.

The October 9 replay-floor correction is adapted from Bertholomus's native
engine commit bdcfd10a2a9091b515e220525d439546ce90de15 in model.py and kernels.py.
The local Python port enables it by default and adds poisoned-ring CUDA and
cold request-order probes. deployment/UPSTREAM-V06.md records the review,
deferred native-engine migration and separate local monitoring changes.


Native Zig migration candidate (October 2026)

This branch extends Bertholomus's native engine at 4e80f05 with separately
sized request windows and shared KV storage, 32 resident slots, bounded
multi-pass drafting, DRM KV allocation, live extent compaction, bounded graph
and prompt-state retention, strict output constraints through xgrammar,
configurable sampling seeds, context aliases and fail-closed rank recovery.
The portable host controller retains ownership journals and reversible display
settings. All qualification claims are scoped in MIGRATION.md; historical
Python performance is not a native-engine measurement.

Native dependency and adaptation notices are in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and
LICENSES/. The source retains Bertholomus, TensorFold, urtho, Jay Leaton,
MiaAI-Lab, Keys, DeepSeek and Emi Huang credits appropriate to their work.
